factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 7 problems
  The reel_script and caption say the arrest happened 'சென்னை அருகே' (near Chennai), but the article gives no such location; the only place mentioned is Kallakurichi.
  The reel_script calls the victim 'அதிகாரி' and describes her in a way that could be read as an identifying detail; the article only says 'பாதிக்கப்பட்ட அதிகாரி' and 'இரும்புப் பெண்மணி', which is acceptable, but the draft adds no name, so this is fine; however the reel_script states that the MLA 'கைது செய்யப்பட்டார்' without the article mentioning who arrested him, which is consistent. No further issue there.
  The caption claims Stalin said ministers and alliance leaders 'எம்எல்ஏவுக்கு ஆதரவாகப் பேசியதாக' (spoke in support of the MLA), which is a paraphrase beyond the article's wording of denying the complaint and issuing 'நடத்தைச் சான்றிதழ்' (character certificates).
  The reel_script says 'அமைச்சர்கள் முதல் கூட்டணிக் கட்சித் தலைவர்கள் வரை புகாரை மறுத்ததாகக் குற்றம் சாட்டினார்' and slide 2 says ministers and alliance leaders 'புகாரை மறுத்தனர்' as fact, omitting that this is Stalin's allegation as reported in the article; the framing is acceptable as attributed, but the slide presents it as a stated fact.
  The reel_script says 'மகளிர் ஆணையம் ஆகியவற்றின் சீற்றத்தால்' (the anger of the women's commission and High Court) led to the arrest, presenting Stalin's claim that the arrest was forced 'வேறு வழியின்றி' as established cause rather than his opinion.
  The article's key fact that the arrest was attributed by Stalin to 'வேறு வழியின்றி' is present, but the slide text 'உயர் நீதிமன்றம், மகளிர் ஆணைய அழுத்தத்தால் கைது நடந்தது' states the cause as fact, which the article only presents as Stalin's view.
  The caption and reel_script describe the posting only as a social media post; the article says the statement was posted 'இன்று' which is not mentioned, a minor omission rather than a factual error.
